-- title:
--   Ends are non-affine Drinfeld places and level moves them, q=3
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime with $q=3$, let $M'\ge 1$ with $q\nmid M'$, and let $\ell$ be a prime with $\ell\equiv 11\pmod{12}$ and $\ell\mid M'$. Let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with residue field $\kappa$, let $F_{ss}$ be a field that is a $\kappa$-algebra, and let $R$ be a regular prolongation of $A$ to $F=$ `fieldBar q M'`, the function field over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ of $X_H$ of level $q^2M'$ with $H$ the kernel of $(\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times\to(\mathbb Z/q)^\times$: a valuation subring `R.integers` of $F$ together with a surjective map `R.residue` onto $F_{ss}$ with kernel the maximal ideal, inducing $\kappa\hookrightarrow F_{ss}$ over $A$, with $A$ the contraction of `R.integers` to $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ and every nonzero $f\in F$ scalable into `R.integers` with nonzero residue. Let $N$ be a finite set of places of $F_{ss}/\kappa$ (valuation subrings, proper, with principal ideals, containing $\kappa$). Assume: `R.integers` is preserved by `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ` for all $\zeta$ a primitive $q$-th root of unity in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ and all $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$; $|N|=q+1$; $N$ is stable under the residue automorphism `R.resAut τ` for every $\tau$ in the subgroup generated by these level automorphisms that preserves `R.integers`. Assume further $\kappa$ is an $\mathbb F_{q^2}$-algebra, the Drinfeld coordinate ring $C_q(\kappa)=\kappa[X_0,X_1]/(\mathrm{drinfeldPoly}-1)$ is a domain, and fix $\zeta$, a subgroup $C_s\le\mu_{q+1}(\mathbb F_{q^2})$ and a $\kappa$-isomorphism $e:F_{ss}\to$ [`DrinfeldCurve.quotField q κ Cs`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelSemistableCoveringW2.html#L32), the fixed field in $\mathrm{Frac}\,C_q(\kappa)$ of the automorphisms attached to $(1,\xi)$, $\xi\in C_s$. Assume the intertwining law: for $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ with `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ⁻¹` preserving `R.integers` and with $(\gamma\bmod q,1)$ in the kernel $H$ of $(g,u)\mapsto\det(g)\,u^{q+1}$, the conjugate by $e$ of `R.resAut (levelAutBar q M' ζ γ⁻¹)` is the action of $(\gamma\bmod q,1)$ on $\mathrm{Frac}\,C_q(\kappa)$. Then (1) a place $Q$ of $F_{ss}/\kappa$ lies off $N$ if and only if for every $z$ in the fixed field whose image in $\mathrm{Frac}\,C_q(\kappa)$ lies in the image of $C_q(\kappa)$ one has $e^{-1}(z)\in Q$; and (2) every $Q\notin N$ satisfies `R.resAut (levelAutBar q M' ζ γ) • Q ≠ Q` for some $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ preserving `R.integers`.
--
--   This identifies the $q+1$ marked places $N$ on a supersingular component of the semistable reduction with the places at infinity of the quotient Drinfeld curve $xy^q-x^qy=1$ modulo $C_s$, the complementary places being exactly the affine ones, and shows that no affine place is fixed by the whole level action. It is the $q=3$ case, at an auxiliary level divisible by a prime $\ell\equiv 11\pmod{12}$, of the corresponding statement for $q\ge 5$, and feeds the transitivity-and-motion statement for ends and smooth places used in the analysis of the supersingular components.
